  "notes": [
    "Every expectation in this file was written by hand from the P5-E2 acceptance criteria, not produced by running the builder. A case says what the controlled-change record must answer; the test then holds the implementation to it.",
    "The base bundle below is the canonical success shape: one Memory run and record, one P5.x identity chain through intent, proposal, edit, candidate, plan and policy version, one passing evidence-complete validation, one explicit acceptance, one declared application outcome, the accepted revision, the revision observed after the rescan, and one current Memory link freshness verdict.",
    "The base bundle's identities are invented but shaped: each carries the prefix its owner actually emits (run:, evidence:, intent:, impact:, edit:, candidate:, bind:, plan:, result:, ws:) and the two digests are 64 hex characters, so a case that changes one is changing an identity of the right shape rather than an arbitrary string.",
    "A case names one or two mutations: set applies a dotted path, drop removes a whole group. Nothing else about the base changes, so a case states exactly what it is about.",
    "The refusal expectations are written out literally, including the code-owned name the reason interpolates. An expectation that repeats the implementation's own constants would prove nothing.",
    "The final two cases differ only in which way the declaration and the observation disagree, because the record must report a contradiction in either direction and must not prefer the operator's word."
  ],
